---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>CrackStreams Privacy Policy – Data Practices & Visitor Details</title>
<meta name="description" content="Explore how CrackStreams addresses visitor privacy, technical information, website activity, cookies, and general data practices across its online platform." />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="top-header">
    <a href="/" class="top-header-title">CrackStreams</a>
  </header>

  <main class="page-container static-content-page">

  <div class="static-content-card">
<h1 class="static-page-title">CrackStreams Privacy &amp; Data Policy</h1>
<p class="static-page-subtitle">Effective date: September 2026</p>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>1. Privacy Principles</h2>

  <p>
    CrackStreams recognizes the importance of responsible information handling. This policy describes
    the general categories of information that may be produced when someone visits the website,
    explains how technical information may support website operations, and outlines the involvement
    of external services that may be accessible through the platform.
  </p>

</section>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>2. Data Associated With Website Access</h2>

  <p>
    Visitors can browse CrackStreams without creating a user account, registering a profile, or
    maintaining a membership. Certain operational information may nevertheless be processed
    automatically as part of delivering web pages, maintaining reliability, identifying technical
    problems, and monitoring general site activity.
  </p>

  <p>
    Information that may be available through normal website access can include:
  </p>

  <ul class="static-list">

    <li>IP address or other network connection details.</li>
    <li>Browser version, device category, and related technical attributes.</li>
    <li>Operating platform, language preference, and configuration details.</li>
    <li>Website pages accessed and broad navigation activity.</li>
    <li>Date and time of access along with referring-site information.</li>

  </ul>

</section>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>3. Cookies, Measurement Tools &amp; External Services</h2>

  <p>
    Certain website components may use cookies, local storage, or similar mechanisms to provide
    requested functionality, retain selected settings, understand technical performance, or assist
    with the operation of individual features. The technologies used on the website may change as
    services and functionality are modified.
  </p>

  <p>
    CrackStreams may also interact with independently operated services through advertisements,
    external links, embedded components, analytics systems, or other integrations. Such providers
    may use their own technologies for collecting or storing information and are governed by their
    respective privacy terms. Visitors should review those policies when interacting with external
    platforms.
  </p>

</section>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>4. Operational Purposes for Collected Information</h2>

  <p>
    Technical information may be useful for keeping the website available, troubleshooting
    unexpected behavior, evaluating broad usage patterns, improving functionality, identifying
    security-related concerns, and maintaining a smoother browsing environment. The website is
    primarily intended to provide access to its pages without requiring visitors to establish a
    personal profile.
  </p>

</section>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>5. Website Security Measures</h2>

  <p>
    Reasonable technical and operational precautions may be used to help maintain the integrity of
    website systems and information generated through ordinary site activity. However, no website,
    network, or internet-based transmission can guarantee absolute protection from every possible
    security risk. Visitors should remain cautious when accessing third-party websites or submitting
    information to services outside CrackStreams.
  </p>

</section>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>6. Independent Websites &amp; Privacy Practices</h2>

  <p>
    CrackStreams may provide links, embedded features, or other connections to services maintained
    by separate organizations. External providers may establish their own policies covering
    cookies, analytics, security procedures, information retention, and other data practices.
    Because these services operate independently, CrackStreams does not determine how they process
    information. Visitors are encouraged to examine the applicable privacy documentation before
    using an outside service or sharing information with it.
  </p>

</section>

<section class="static-section">

  <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>

  <p>
    This policy can be revised when website features, technologies, or internal procedures change.
    Any new version will be published on this page and accompanied by an updated effective or
    revision date. Questions concerning privacy or website information practices may be submitted
    through the <a href="/contact" class="inline-link">Contact Page</a>.
  </p>

</section>

  </div>

</main>

</body>
</html>